--- WHAT THE SURFACE REPRODUCES (parity with the web source) ---
  - Per-location key = "teslasync.scroll:" + pathname + search (web keyFor / STORAGE_PREFIX).
  - POP (back/forward): restore the saved offset, or the top when unseen (web `saved ?? 0`).
  - PUSH / REPLACE: a fresh navigation always starts at the top (web setScrollTop(target, 0)).
  - Continuous capture of the scroll offset per location, coalesced to one write per frame (web rAF throttle).
  - Final flush of the position on navigation away and on unmount (web capture-effect cleanup).
  - Renders null: invisible behavioural coordinator — no chrome, no static copy, NO i18n keys, no interactive
    elements. There is no loading/empty/error/stale/offline state because the web source has no data fetch
    (same reasoning as the approved RouteAnnouncer predecessor); the modelled states are mount, continuous
    capture, POP restore and PUSH/REPLACE reset, each unit-tested.

  Files (4-file surface pattern):
    ScrollRestoration.Model.cs      Registration (slug, storage key), ScrollNavigationKind, the four P1/S8 seam
                                    interfaces, the pure ScrollRestorationProjection, ScrollRestorationDiagnostics.
    ScrollRestoration.Source.cs     InMemoryScrollOffsetStore (sessionStorage analogue, non-finite guard) +
                                    MutableScrollLocationSource (shell-driven useLocation/useNavigationType binding).
    ScrollRestoration.ViewModel.cs  UI-thread-free capture/restore state holder (the Microsoft.UI-free logic).
    ScrollRestoration.cs            Invisible WinUI ContentControl + ScrollViewer/CompositionTarget adapters
                                    (the bare WinUI view; exercised by the app build, excluded from headless tests).

